From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: h713 <h713@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: make the self-managed regulatory domain settable

The wiphy is self-managed, so cfg80211's regulatory.db never applies to it.
rwnx_custregd() installs a domain from this driver's own regdb.c instead,
chosen by default_ccode -- which was a compiled-in "00" with no way to
change it short of editing the source.

"00" resolves to a permissive world entry: 2380-2520 MHz and 5140-5980 MHz
at 20 dBm with DFS-UNSET, no NO_IR and no passive-scan.  That is wider than
the ISM band and covers DFS and weather-radar spectrum with no DFS
constraint, and it is what the radio actually ran under.

The driver's own table is fine -- 185 countries, 98 distinct rule sets, with
correct DFS regions, NO_IR/NO_OUTDOOR flags and per-subband power limits.
Only the selector was stuck.  Expose it as a module parameter so the
operating domain can be set at load time.

---
 aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_mod_params.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++

--- a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_mod_params.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_mod_params.c
@@ -237,6 +237,27 @@
 char default_ccode[4] = "00";
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * The wiphy is self-managed (custregd), so cfg80211's regulatory.db never
+ * applies to it -- rwnx_custregd() installs a domain from this driver's own
+ * table in regdb.c instead, selected by default_ccode.  That table is real:
+ * 185 countries, 98 distinct rule sets, with correct DFS regions, NO_IR and
+ * NO_OUTDOOR flags and per-subband power limits.
+ *
+ * The compiled-in default is "00", which resolves to a permissive world entry
+ * that advertises 2380-2520 MHz and 5140-5980 MHz at 20 dBm with DFS-UNSET --
+ * wider than the ISM band and covering DFS and weather-radar spectrum with no
+ * DFS or passive-scan constraint.  There was no way to change it without a
+ * rebuild, so every board shipped transmitting under those rules.
+ *
+ * Expose it so the operating domain can be set at module load:
+ *   options aic8800_fdrv default_ccode=US
+ */
+module_param_string(default_ccode, default_ccode, sizeof(default_ccode),
+		    S_IRUGO);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(default_ccode,
+		 "ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 regulatory domain for the self-managed wiphy (default: 00, permissive world)");
+
 char country_code[4];
 module_param_string(country_code, country_code, 4, 0600);
 
